#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092021 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbf5fbb2-688a-5833-87b9-37229c8fb692" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Characteristic Equation of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "aebe3048-cc5b-5340-a15e-d577ae2ee72a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5479" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I$:\n﻿﻿﻿$\\begin{bmatrix}2 - λ & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2 - λ\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A - λI) &= 0 \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix}2 - λ & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2 - λ\\end{vmatrix} &= 0 \\\\\n(2 - λ)(2 - λ) - 4 \\cdot 3 &= 0 \\\\\n4 - 4λ + λ^{2} - 12 &= 0 \\\\\nλ^{2} - 4λ - 8 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092022 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With At Most One Distinct Eigenvalue"}] :question/id #uuid "55e695b2-4581-5ba7-9604-506234b88323" :question/math-academy-id "e-5480" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $B-\\lambda I$:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 - λ & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 - λ\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation\n\n$$\n\\det(B-\\lambda I) = 0\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(B - λI) &= 0 \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix}4 - λ & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 - λ\\end{vmatrix} &= 0 \\\\\n(4 - λ)(4 - λ) - 0 \\cdot 0 &= 0 \\\\\n(λ - 4)^{2} &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $B$ has only one eigenvalue $\\lambda=4$, which is a double root of the characteristic equation.\n\n**Note:** We also say that $\\lambda=4$ has an **algebraic multiplicity** of $2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092023 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "864cf210-cbb0-5a79-b90a-33a5df332559" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With Two Distinct Eigenvalues"}] :question/id #uuid "a42d0af8-869c-5c2a-8182-22b14b9546e2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5481" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I$:\n﻿﻿$\\begin{bmatrix}10 - λ & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7 - λ\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation\n\n$$\n\\det(A-\\lambda I) = 0\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A - λI) &= 0 \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix}10 - λ & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7 - λ\\end{vmatrix} &= 0 \\\\\n(10 - λ)(7 - λ) - 3 \\cdot 6 &= 0 \\\\\n70 - 7λ - 10λ + λ^{2} - 18 &= 0 \\\\\nλ^{2} - 17λ + 52 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= (17 ± \\sqrt{(-17)^{2} - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 52})/(2 \\cdot 1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{17 ± \\sqrt{81}}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{17 ± 9}{2} \\\\\n&= 13, 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda=13$ and $\\lambda=4$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092024 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a Triangular/Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "9e40836e-18e9-5df6-a930-05875b920335" :question/math-academy-id "e-5482" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I$:\n﻿﻿﻿$\\begin{bmatrix}3 - λ & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\sqrt{3} - λ\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation\n\n$$\n\\det (A - \\lambda I) = 0\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A - λI) &= 0 \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix}3 - λ & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\sqrt{3} - λ\\end{vmatrix} &= 0 \\\\\n(3 - λ)(-2\\sqrt{3} - λ) - 9 \\cdot 0 &= 0 \\\\\n(λ - 3)(λ + 2\\sqrt{3}) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the eigenvalues\n\n$$\n\\lambda={\\color{red}3}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\lambda={\\color{blue}-2\\sqrt{3}}\n$$\n\nIf we look again at the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\nwe see that the eigenvalues are the entries on the main diagonal. This is true in general: the eigenvalues of a *triangular* or *diagonal* matrix are *always* given by the entries on the main diagonal!\n\n**Watch out!** For a general matrix (which is neither triangular nor diagonal), this might not be the case!"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092462 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a Triangular/Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cbcb05c-0d49-5cbd-80eb-6b804f107249" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = \\sqrt{3}$ and $λ = 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089209} {:answer/id #uuid "0a494e60-093c-58c4-a59c-aa2a3b60e7e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089210} {:answer/id #uuid "323c248b-e18e-5611-b08d-9631fd900654" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ =-2$ and $λ = \\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089211} {:answer/id #uuid "479da784-7457-5ebe-ab3e-66bcab6eacf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ =-2$ and $λ =-\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089212} {:answer/id #uuid "5016ca94-d6c8-5940-9a53-df997f015259" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = 4$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cbcb05c-0d49-5cbd-80eb-6b804f107249" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = \\sqrt{3}$ and $λ = 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089209} :answer-field/id #uuid "aed5cf4f-5cf4-5caf-81e8-f22caef29322" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089208}] :question/id #uuid "b1fb4b20-223a-5224-b15e-06a76416065c" :question/math-academy-id "q-11983" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294524 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "864cf210-cbb0-5a79-b90a-33a5df332559" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With Two Distinct Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "958eb313-8eb6-5031-a652-a4e5dd9925fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294526} {:answer/id #uuid "9a2c98c8-dde6-5160-860d-95f972eed39f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$  (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294527} {:answer/id #uuid "86c421c8-23b5-5b82-9614-79651e5ebf72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294528} {:answer/id #uuid "1199a2e1-6452-5f3c-adbc-e5506a0a9b81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294529} {:answer/id #uuid "b625c85e-ad5b-5b27-99e8-54f4d0d6d292" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b625c85e-ad5b-5b27-99e8-54f4d0d6d292" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294530} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1d8f83f-93a5-5a9a-bb8f-efe63bf1e4f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2a59a38-6b0a-5bff-ab4c-adc26ea6a0e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-12296" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$S=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $S-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nS-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-8-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ -5 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(S-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-8-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ -5 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-8-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-4\\cdot (-5) & =0 \\\\ -32+8\\lambda -4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+20 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda -12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-4\\pm \\sqrt{{4}^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 12}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4\\pm \\sqrt{64}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4\\pm 8}{2} \\\\  & =-6,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092636 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbf5fbb2-688a-5833-87b9-37229c8fb692" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Characteristic Equation of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ee9bc6f-5a72-5add-8ecc-1b71282a0419" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ^{2} - 1 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090282} {:answer/id #uuid "c9d2940b-62bd-566f-a82a-fd40ff14c2ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ^{2} + 4λ + 4 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090283} {:answer/id #uuid "175f4c67-f0a6-5f3f-b81c-431534fbf93d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ^{2} - 4λ - 4 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090284} {:answer/id #uuid "57b0c675-56c8-59fd-a95d-6833904978ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ^{2} - 4λ + 4 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090285} {:answer/id #uuid "6221c02d-d3ab-509e-9bb6-056de1d0571f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ^{2} + 3λ + 9 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9d2940b-62bd-566f-a82a-fd40ff14c2ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ^{2} + 4λ + 4 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090283} :answer-field/id #uuid "f641e017-3fcd-5a0a-a1e7-e9e7601b5fca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090281}] :question/id #uuid "21a76447-bb7c-5d72-a771-38739632e899" :question/math-academy-id "q-36758" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix $A = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With At Most One Distinct Eigenvalue"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af44a87e-26da-5096-85ff-780ae0baf3eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = 8$ and $λ = 5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090294} {:answer/id #uuid "d645007a-712e-567d-9277-c4aa59d7d840" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = 8$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090295} {:answer/id #uuid "fa6f39b7-0975-5673-b988-9d3fd267b722" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ =-6$ and $λ =-10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090296} {:answer/id #uuid "20eefca5-71cc-5e10-82b4-6391ca5fba54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090297} {:answer/id #uuid "232e2323-0dca-511f-8115-f44c3edf1827" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = 6$ and $λ = 10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20eefca5-71cc-5e10-82b4-6391ca5fba54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090297} :answer-field/id #uuid "40774c4b-45e1-57e2-b84f-15814ca61892" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090293}] :question/id #uuid "f563abe4-0d8d-5d69-9a75-20dcd9079f0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-36776" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n\n$Q = \\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -10\\end{bmatrix}$."}]}
